  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe EIP-712 `DOMAIN_SEPARATOR` is a critical security mechanism designed to prevent a signature created for one protocol from being re-used on another. It achieves this by creating a unique fingerprint for the contract.\n\nIn implementation, the `DOMAIN_SEPARATOR` is calculated in the constructor and stored as an immutable variable. This calculation permanently captures and hard-codes the `block.chainid` that was present at the time of deployment.\n\nHowever, the `_verifyAndMarkIntent` function uses live `chainid()` when calculating the separate `intentHash`.\n\n[**Code Snippet**](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-sequence/blob/593987c2b569f3212d2cadb31fc8d14b84bc30a9/src/TrailsIntentEntrypoint.sol#L65)\n```solidity\nconstructor() {\n        DOMAIN_SEPARATOR = keccak256(\n            abi.encode(\n                keccak256(\"EIP712Domain(string name,string version,uint256 chainId,address verifyingContract)\"),\n                keccak256(bytes(\"TrailsIntentEntrypoint\")),\n                keccak256(bytes(VERSION)),\n@>              block.chainid,\n                address(this)\n            )\n        );\n    }\n\nfunction _verifyAndMarkIntent(\n        address user,\n        address token,\n        uint256 amount,\n        address intentAddress,\n        uint256 deadline,\n        uint256 nonce,\n        uint256 feeAmount,\n        address feeCollector,\n        uint8 sigV,\n        bytes32 sigR,\n        bytes32 sigS\n    ) internal {\n        ...\n        assembly {\n            let ptr := mload(0x40)\n            mstore(ptr, _typehash)\n            mstore(add(ptr, 0x20), user)\n            mstore(add(ptr, 0x40), token)\n            mstore(add(ptr, 0x60), amount)\n            mstore(add(ptr, 0x80), intentAddress)\n            mstore(add(ptr, 0xa0), deadline)\n@>          mstore(add(ptr, 0xc0), chainid())\n            mstore(add(ptr, 0xe0), nonce)\n            mstore(add(ptr, 0x100), feeAmount)\n            mstore(add(ptr, 0x120), feeCollector)\n            intentHash := keccak256(ptr, 0x140)\n        }\n\n@>      bytes32 _domainSeparator = DOMAIN_SEPARATOR;\n        bytes32 digest;\n        assembly {\n            let ptr := mload(0x40)\n            mstore(ptr, 0x1901)\n@>          mstore(add(ptr, 0x20), _domainSeparator)\n            mstore(add(ptr, 0x40), intentHash)\n            digest := keccak256(add(ptr, 0x1e), 0x42)\n        }\n@>      address recovered = ECDSA.recover(digest, sigV, sigR, sigS);\n        if (recovered != user) revert InvalidIntentSignature();\n        \n        ...\n    }\n```\n\nIf the network undergoes a hard fork or an L2 upgrade that changes its `chainid`, a significant mismatch occurs. The contract attempts to validate the signature by calculating a `digest` from two conflicting data sources:\n\na) The `DOMAIN_SEPARATOR`, which is stale and hard-coded with the old `chainid` from its immutable slot.\n\nb) The `intentHash`, which is calculated live using the new `chainid()` opcode.\n\nThe `digest` calculated by the contract (using a mix of old and new chain IDs) will never match the digest signed by the user (using only the new chain ID). As a result, `ECDSA.recover` will always fail, and the `InvalidIntentSignature` error will be triggered on every call. This permanently bricks both `depositToIntent` and `depositToIntentWithPermit`, leading to a total Denial of Service (DoS) for the protocol. Given the system uses multiple chains and the contract is non-upgradeable, the high likelihood of future chain ID changes combined with the impact of a permanent DoS results in a Medium severity.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nThe `DOMAIN_SEPARATOR` should not be stored as immutable. It should be recalculated dynamically to ensure it always uses the current, live `chainid`.\n\nConsider replacing the immutable `DOMAIN_SEPARATOR` variable and the constructor logic with an internal view function:\n\n```solidity\nfunction _domainSeparator() internal view returns (bytes32) {\n    return keccak256(\n        abi.encode(\n            keccak256(\"EIP712Domain(string name,string version,uint256 chainId,address verifyingContract)\"),\n            keccak256(bytes(\"TrailsIntentEntrypoint\")),\n            keccak256(bytes(VERSION)),\n            block.chainid, // Use live chainid\n            address(this)\n        )\n    );\n}\n```\n\nThen, in `_verifyAndMarkIntent`, replace the immutable variable with a call to this function:\n\n```solidity\n-   bytes32 _domainSeparator = DOMAIN_SEPARATOR;\n+   bytes32 _domainSeparator = _domainSeparator();\n```",
